.TH CRS-GUI 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-controlroom-setup 1.0.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
crs\-gui \- Mu2e control\-room manager window: tunnels and service discovery
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crs\-gui
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
PyQt6 window with two tabs.
.SS Tunnels
One row per configured session with host, account, display, local port
and tunnel state, and Open, Close and Connect buttons, plus Open all,
Close all and Refresh.
State is re\-probed every 15 s.
Each action runs in a
.B QThread
and reports back by signal; the operations are those of
.BR crs\-tunnel (1).
.SS Discovery
Lists responders to a mu2edaq\-discovery DISCOVER: name, app, host,
port, started, pid, id.
.TP
.B Via gateway
(default) runs
.B "~/controlroom/bin/mu2edaq\-discover \-\-json || mu2edaq\-discover \-\-json"
over ssh on the selected
.IB account @ host
and parses its JSON.
Nothing in this package installs
.B mu2edaq\-discover
on the hosts; it must already be on the non\-interactive PATH there.
.TP
.B Local multicast
calls
.B mu2edaq_discovery.discover()
in this process with the configured group, port and timeout; requires
the package in the venv
.RB ( bootstrap.sh
installs the sibling checkout).
.PP
Double\-clicking a row whose app is
.B vnc
maps its host and port to a configured session, opens the tunnel and
starts the viewer.
That tunnel open runs on the UI thread, so the window freezes for the
duration of the ssh authentication.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
.IR controlroom.yaml ;
see
.BR crs\-tunnel (1).
.SH FILES
.I ~/.crs/ssh\-ctrl\-*
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR CRS_CONFIG ,
.BR CRS_GATEWAY .
.SH EXIT STATUS
The Qt event loop's code, normally 0; 1 after a configuration error
dialog.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
venv/bin/crs\-gui
venv/bin/crs\-gui \-\-config ~/my\-controlroom.yaml
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR crs\-tunnel (1),
.BR crs\-remote (1),
.BR vnc\-discovery\-responder.py (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-discover (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ group.
